## FINDINGS (ordered by severity)

**F1 — CRITICAL. The frozen claim set is not machine-verifiable.**
Three independent defects in `saner_rene_claim_matrix_v1.json`: (a) the file does not parse — two bare path strings follow the closing brace of the root object; (b) `evidence_hashes` covers 8 files while the claims cite at least 12, and the two hash keys that do map to FinQA/design audits use short names (`finqa_formal_v3_recompute_audit.md`, `causal_checkpoint_design_audit.md`) that do not match the cited `docs/experiments/2026-10-10_…` / `2026-10-11_…` paths, so hash-to-path binding is not mechanical; (c) the single most load-bearing FinQA document — the `MEASUREMENT_OBJECT_MISMATCH` autopsy — appears only in the dangling fragment and is unhashed, as are `stage_e_observability_metrics_v1.md`, `checkpoint_discrimination_tables_v2.json`, `t2_visibility_sensitivity.json`, `finqa_v2_formal_v3_activation_record_v1.md`. Also unhashed: the corpus and injection-map digests that §4.1 does state (good) but the matrix does not carry. **Consequence:** C3's interpretive layer is `UNVERIFIED` regardless of its merits.

**F2 — CRITICAL. Contribution 3 is worded above its evidence, and it contradicts the current paper body.**
The scope lock and Version-B commit the paper to "controlled localization" / "ablation demonstrates that localization disappears", while the same packet admits the features are "contract-derived and perfectly separable by construction", labels the ablation `exploratory`, and the actual draft (§3.1, RR-17, §6.1, Conclusion) still says localization is **unestablished** because only one leaf responds. The readiness SUPERSEDED note adopts multi-leaf on 2026-10-11, but RR-12/RR-17 (dated 2026-10-04) still say "only future work" and the pending-advisor-decision list still offers "multi-leaf versus second dataflow" as open. The frozen packet therefore contains two mutually inconsistent claim states.

**F3 — HIGH. FinQA causal attribution and undefined formal vocabulary.**
"Because measurement objects were not causally aligned" (scope lock Limitations) and "requires causal alignment" (C3, thesis) are causal/conditional-universal claims from a single failed transfer with an undefined sample (n=89) and an undefined result class (`SECOND_FLOW_MIXED`). Route B's stop rationale adds two more undefined terms ("M aliasing", "R/N downstream non-estimability") — and "M aliasing" sits in visible tension with a contribution that reports perfect M/R/N stage separation at LOCO 1.0. Until the terms are defined, the reader cannot tell whether these are the same measurement objects.

**F4 — HIGH. The machine-readable forbidden list is weaker than the human one.**
The matrix omits the harmfulness-overreach prohibition. Harmfulness is simultaneously the weakest-evidence area (28 cases, one judge, two of six families with zero calls, primary definition still an open advisor decision) and the only area where a forbidden-claim breach would be easy to commit silently by an automated gate.

**F5 — HIGH. Deficit framing on the headline number.**
"Blindness" / "blind spot" appears in the title, the thesis, §5.1 and §6.1 as a settled characterization, while §3.2 defines the observed mechanism as *silent absorption via normalization* and §2.3 explicitly requires distinguishing evaluator blindness from "mutants whose intended effect is not represented on the scored observation surface". The paper states the distinction and then does not apply it to its own headline.

**F6 — MEDIUM-HIGH. Statistical reporting that will not survive arithmetic.**
Pooled 0.7766 ≠ mean of printed rates (0.7762); two per-seed rates are not integer counts of 95; the pooled CI is consistent with 285 independent trials over the same 95 tables; table-level CIs reproduce under no standard estimator; the matching ceiling compares 20/21 to 40/67; the 2,382-record clean set is unconstructed; the affine slope is "approximately" 0.375 against an exact threshold identity. Each is individually minor; collectively they are what a careful reviewer uses to discredit the whole quantitative layer.

**F7 — MEDIUM. Governance/state drift across the frozen packet.**
Three titles; scope lock still advertises "Optional route: B / READ_ONLY_48H_QUALIFICATION" while the matrix says `STOP_BRANCH`; readiness lists two pending advisor decisions though one is superseded; check counts drift 73 → 74; the internal `claim_manifest_v1.json` carries **5** claims while the SANER matrix carries **3**, with no mapping between them; the readiness file's 2026-09-22 receipt says Office visual check incomplete while the 2026-10-03 addendum closes it (resolved, but a first-pass reader is misled).

**F8 — MEDIUM. Compound claim IDs.**
C1 bundles a definitional claim, an empirical profile, and a harmfulness boundary. C2 bundles a structural result, an identifiability result, and an instrumentation requirement of three different evidential strengths. C3 bundles an empirical autopsy, an interpretive label, and a design requirement. A reviewer can defeat one clause and make the ID look partially failed. Split before freeze.

**F9 — MEDIUM. Content outside the frozen role boundaries.**
§5.5 (Stage R gated/ungated boundary case) is in the paper body but is authorised by no scope-lock role (which lists only FinQA, multi-leaf, NIST, ITIL). Version-B's own decision line allows only "evidence-table/figure production" with "no paper-body edit without user review" — so the multi-leaf contribution cannot be merged into the body without an explicit review gate.

**F10 — LOW-MEDIUM. Uncited external framing and figure status labels.**
NIST/TEVV framing has no entry in the reference list. Figure 3 Panel A presents controlled cells (1.0/1.0) beside an exploratory cell (0.3333) with no status labels. RR-07 (unverified venue labels) remains correctly bounded to `arXiv preprint` placeholders.

**F11 — LOW. Internal-consistency positives worth preserving** (recorded so they are not "fixed" away): 96+22=118 and all per-family sums close; the six printed detection rates reproduce; both OCR exact intervals reproduce as two-sided Clopper-Pearson; 5 parsing + 7 QA = 12 leaves; the "0.81 to 1.00" family range matches the per-family table (0.8125–1.00); the 112>96 and 20-vs-13 paradoxes are both explicitly defused; the two-estimand OCR disclosure is exemplary practice.

