## VERDICT: CHALLENGE_CLAIM_SET

Scope of the challenge, stated precisely so it is not misread as a refutation of the measurements:

**Endorsed as-is (with the wording narrowing already listed):** the C1 construct separation; the family-visibility quantification including the OCR 0/13 boundary with its two estimands; the C2 structural affine/rank statement and the clean-only matched-FPR non-identifiability result; the weight-search informative null; the judge-calibration disclosure.

**Challenged — not citable as currently worded:** (i) the frozen claim-matrix artifact itself (malformed, incomplete hash coverage, hash keys not bound to paths) — F1; (ii) contribution 3's positive framing ("controlled localization", "demonstrates", "perfectly separable") and its contradiction with the current draft body — F2; (iii) the FinQA causal "because", the phrase "not protocol blindness", and the undefined `SECOND_FLOW_MIXED` / "M aliasing" / "R/N downstream non-estimability" vocabulary — F3; (iv) the "blindness" deficit framing of the headline — F5; (v) the omission of the harmfulness prohibition from the machine-readable forbidden list — F4.

This is a challenge to the **admissibility of the claim set as worded and anchored**, not to the underlying measured quantities, several of which survive independent arithmetic checking inside the packet.

